<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Solomonic dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">from <a href="/years/1270">1270</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Solomonic</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Solomonic dynasty ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> from 1270, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yekuno-amlak">Yekuno Amlak</a> overthrew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagwe-dynasty">Zagwe dynasty</a>, until the deposition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haile-selassie">Haile Selassie</a> in 1974. It claimed descent from King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/queen-of-sheba">Queen of Sheba</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a> describe this lineage as a basis of royal legitimacy alongside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox Church</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/solomonic-dynasty.jpg" alt="Solomonic dynasty" width="320" height="357" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Imperial_coat_of_arms_of_Ethiopia_(Haile_Selassie).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>Solomonic dynasty</b> was established in 1270, traditionally on 10 August, when Yekuno Amlak overthrew the last Zagwe king at the Battle of Ansata, claiming descent from King Solomon and the Queen of Sheba to legitimise his seizure of power.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
